.. _`speedwalk filter`:

SPEEDWALK FILTER
================

This is totally new to Lyntin.  What happens is that the user input
is checked to see if it's a speedwalk expression.  If it is, then it
is expanded into speedwalk commands and then recursed over.

Tintin implemented speedwalking, but it was pretty limited.  Lyntin
implemented speedwalking that is very complex and allows you to do
many many things including building speedwalk dirs that get expanded
into Lyntin aliases.

